WEBVTT

01:00.390 --> 01:07.230
It is said that 70% of the
human brain's capacity is unused.

01:09.240 --> 01:11.300
It's also thought that...

01:11.870 --> 01:15.070
...the mysterious powers that humans
have are hidden in this part of the brain.

01:17.010 --> 01:21.570
The 70% of the brain that is not used...

01:22.350 --> 01:24.080
...is often called this...

01:24.150 --> 01:29.890
<i>Night Head Genesis</i>

01:38.370 --> 01:39.530
Is that the place?

01:39.600 --> 01:40.090
Yeah.

01:48.070 --> 01:48.970
Come out.

01:54.050 --> 01:55.240
Those guys...

01:55.650 --> 01:56.810
...killed...

01:56.980 --> 01:57.970
...my dog.

02:00.750 --> 02:03.690
They hit and killed
my dog as they escaped.

02:07.430 --> 02:09.120
He was my friend.

02:09.960 --> 02:11.400
I loved him.

02:13.230 --> 02:14.330
Those guys...

02:15.370 --> 02:17.730
Don't say anything. Please...

02:18.170 --> 02:20.160
It shouldn't be considered a crime.

02:20.240 --> 02:21.970
We should contact Mikuriya.

02:22.110 --> 02:23.010
Yeah...

02:23.580 --> 02:25.600
What? What are you going to do?

02:25.980 --> 02:29.380
I think it's best for him to be put in
custody of someone named Mikuriya.

02:29.680 --> 02:30.650
Put in custody!?

02:30.720 --> 02:33.550
What do you mean by put in custody!
I won't let him go anywhere!

02:34.150 --> 02:37.280
I won't... I won't let
something like that happen!

02:37.760 --> 02:40.850
Are you fine with letting
this boy kill more people?

02:44.160 --> 02:45.690
He's kind...

02:45.900 --> 02:48.130
He's a kind and good child...

02:49.270 --> 02:53.070
It's just that the people in
this world didn't leave him alone.

02:53.570 --> 02:54.800
Isn't that right?

02:54.980 --> 02:56.530
Poor thing...

02:58.110 --> 03:02.510
There are moments everyone
thinks that person should die.

03:02.820 --> 03:05.550
If you're human, everyone thinks that.

03:05.790 --> 03:08.190
But they don't have
powers like this child...

03:08.260 --> 03:10.280
...so they're able to live a normal life.

03:12.230 --> 03:13.420
Isn't that right?

03:24.570 --> 03:25.730
Brother!

03:47.330 --> 03:48.990
It's that girl...

03:54.130 --> 03:55.340
<i>Recollection</i>

03:55.340 --> 03:59.140
<i>Recollection
Episode 8</i>

04:01.270 --> 04:03.670
3 weeks later in the afternoon...

04:03.840 --> 04:07.300
...2 brothers are going to
come to the front of the house.

04:07.380 --> 04:08.710
What?

04:09.680 --> 04:11.120
Shouko?

04:21.660 --> 04:23.820
Where did you go?

04:49.920 --> 04:54.120
We met this boy at the
campgrounds last summer.

04:54.630 --> 04:56.960
He got very attached to Shouko.

04:57.500 --> 05:01.700
The mother really wanted a
picture of the two of them together.

05:02.340 --> 05:07.070
Shouko asked my husband to send
the pictures to that boy's home...

05:31.100 --> 05:32.560
Were you able to find something out?

05:32.630 --> 05:33.890
No...

05:34.170 --> 05:36.600
I couldn't read
anything off of the photo.

05:37.870 --> 05:39.630
Shouko Futami, huh?

05:40.170 --> 05:43.700
So that girl actually has disappeared
from the real world too.

05:44.510 --> 05:46.100
I wonder where she is...

05:46.550 --> 05:48.140
I don't even have a clue.

06:00.530 --> 06:02.360
It was true...

06:04.700 --> 06:10.290
Shouko said to be here at this time
and I would be able to see you guys.

06:20.080 --> 06:25.640
These are hieroglyphs found in
Easter Island called Rongorongo.

06:25.820 --> 06:29.550
But apparently there are letters
that were never seen before and...

06:29.620 --> 06:33.060
...they didn't think that
they had much meaning.

06:35.090 --> 06:35.920
How is it?

06:36.000 --> 06:37.260
Did you find out anything?

06:39.870 --> 06:42.730
But these letters
have a strange power.

06:43.840 --> 06:47.530
When you stare at it for a long time,
it's like you are being dragged in.

06:53.250 --> 06:57.340
Elder Misaki went on a journey
away from this world.

06:57.720 --> 07:00.080
That's why the barrier disappeared.

07:01.250 --> 07:03.850
"Tonight, 2 brothers will escape."

07:04.720 --> 07:08.420
That's what Shouko said and
she gave this notebook to me.

07:08.800 --> 07:09.920
Other than that...

07:10.000 --> 07:13.760
Other than that, did she
say anything about us?

07:17.840 --> 07:20.070
Shouko disappeared once in a while.

07:20.140 --> 07:21.300
Disappeared?

07:21.640 --> 07:24.970
If I was talking about a book I liked,
she would all of a sudden disappear...

07:25.040 --> 07:27.980
...and when she got back,
she was at that bookstore.

07:28.050 --> 07:32.250
When we were together in my room,
all of a sudden she'd disappear...

07:32.320 --> 07:34.720
...then I get a phone call and
she'd already be back at her house.

07:34.790 --> 07:39.990
But I thought no one would believe me
if I said that, so I kept quiet about it.

07:40.690 --> 07:46.000
Every time she came back,
she talked about a lot of things to me.

07:47.530 --> 07:48.300
What?

07:49.640 --> 07:52.160
I met this very ancient person...

07:52.240 --> 07:53.540
What do you mean ancient?

07:53.610 --> 07:54.630
Um...

07:54.870 --> 07:57.840
So ancient that they're not
in the history textbooks.

07:59.750 --> 08:01.340
I saw space too.

08:01.880 --> 08:03.250
Shouko...

08:03.980 --> 08:08.320
A long time ago, all different kinds
of people came from space...

08:08.390 --> 08:10.480
...and started living on earth.

08:12.360 --> 08:17.350
Shouko said those things
like they were normal.

08:18.000 --> 08:21.560
She said whatever I say to
you guys, you'd believe me.

08:21.970 --> 08:25.960
The two of you are a little more
advanced than normal people, so...

08:26.040 --> 08:30.030
...you suffered and
were hurt because of that.

08:31.040 --> 08:37.780
But, you two are an essential existence
for the big reformation that's coming.

08:38.820 --> 08:39.880
Reformation?

08:40.350 --> 08:42.150
Shouko was saying that.

08:42.420 --> 08:44.320
A big reformation...

08:44.660 --> 08:46.630
Yes, that's what she said.

08:50.860 --> 08:51.730
Miss Miki?

08:52.870 --> 08:55.600
It's a transition period
for a while here on.

08:55.700 --> 09:00.260
For a human to get closer from
a materialistic state to a mental state...

09:00.340 --> 09:02.330
...complication is required.

09:02.940 --> 09:05.970
Don't forget this...

09:06.280 --> 09:10.580
Not everything is flowing
towards the positive!

09:18.960 --> 09:21.690
You guys bear a grudge
toward this world.

09:22.130 --> 09:25.290
This world that has
made you outcasts.

09:25.570 --> 09:29.190
You also bear a grudge
on your parents, I know.

09:29.370 --> 09:33.070
The truth is you guys want to
see your parents and kill them.

09:33.140 --> 09:34.630
Cut it out! Shut up!

09:34.910 --> 09:37.970
Your existence attracts bad things.

09:38.140 --> 09:42.580
Your existence is stupid, ignorant,
and you can't do anything about!

09:46.790 --> 09:51.880
Look, you showed your
true colors as a monster, huh?

09:52.460 --> 09:53.550
Stop it!

10:10.580 --> 10:11.300
Brother!

10:39.540 --> 10:40.770
I'm right here.

10:40.840 --> 10:41.860
Right here.

11:12.340 --> 11:13.360
Miss Miki!

11:14.810 --> 11:15.970
What is going on?

11:16.040 --> 11:17.300
The cup is...

11:17.610 --> 11:19.370
What happened? Are you hurt?

11:19.480 --> 11:20.610
Miss Miki!

11:21.050 --> 11:22.380
G-Get the ambulance!

11:22.450 --> 11:23.310
Yes!

11:25.920 --> 11:26.940
Miss Miki!

11:29.290 --> 11:31.690
The memories are not lies.

11:31.760 --> 11:32.620
What?

11:33.190 --> 11:36.860
Your childhood memories are not lies.

11:38.000 --> 11:39.090
Miss Miki!

11:55.820 --> 11:57.870
We are essential existences?

11:58.890 --> 12:01.250
I had never thought of that at all.

12:02.160 --> 12:06.220
The day Shouko disappeared was
the day we escaped from that place.

12:07.760 --> 12:09.730
She knew that.

12:10.000 --> 12:13.860
That Elder Misaki created
a barrier in that forest.

12:13.930 --> 12:17.370
And how we couldn't
get out because of that...

12:17.500 --> 12:18.330
Yeah...

12:20.370 --> 12:23.770
She also knew that we
were going to come see Miki.

12:26.610 --> 12:28.510
Who was that guy?

12:30.680 --> 12:32.510
The memories are not lies?

13:01.050 --> 13:03.020
Then why isn't our
home there anymore!

13:03.080 --> 13:04.710
What was with that guy!

13:05.080 --> 13:06.110
Brother...

13:06.220 --> 13:08.410
Something is moving along with us.

13:08.920 --> 13:09.950
Something...

13:32.580 --> 13:33.810
Please tell us...

13:33.980 --> 13:35.810
What do you mean by transition?

13:36.850 --> 13:40.050
What do you mean by
essential existence for the transition?

13:41.390 --> 13:45.480
I still don't even
comprehend my own self.

13:45.860 --> 13:49.620
I am within the "bend"
that leads to all of the world.

13:51.060 --> 13:53.930
There isn't time or distance here.

13:55.000 --> 13:59.460
So I can't see many things
at once and feel them also.

13:59.940 --> 14:02.460
Then, please answer my question.

14:04.440 --> 14:05.670
I don't know.

14:05.780 --> 14:08.710
Then what about the
message you left us?

14:09.120 --> 14:11.110
Those weren't my words.

14:11.520 --> 14:13.140
Whose words were they?

14:13.590 --> 14:15.210
They're no one's words.

14:18.790 --> 14:20.050
She's disappearing.

14:22.360 --> 14:25.420
That man pulls us closer.

14:26.730 --> 14:28.960
That man... to Miki...

14:34.010 --> 14:35.060
What did she say!

14:35.170 --> 14:40.910
He's trying to kill Miki and
make our sadness his own power.

14:41.680 --> 14:43.620
Please protect Miki.

14:47.190 --> 14:50.280
We attracted that guy?

14:53.630 --> 14:57.260
<i>Hospital</i>

14:59.730 --> 15:01.170
You're awake?

15:04.000 --> 15:05.300
Mother...

15:05.670 --> 15:07.970
The doctor said it's anemia.

15:10.010 --> 15:11.670
I'm fine now.

15:11.880 --> 15:13.780
I'm sorry to make you worry.

15:13.850 --> 15:15.940
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

15:16.020 --> 15:17.480
Are you thirsty?

15:17.580 --> 15:18.710
You want to drink something?

15:18.780 --> 15:20.150
Thank you.

15:29.130 --> 15:30.100
Mother?

16:09.300 --> 16:11.790
I'll show you the lost past.

16:11.900 --> 16:13.630
You guys' past!

16:15.310 --> 16:16.330
Miss Miki!

16:38.700 --> 16:39.320
Hey!

16:39.700 --> 16:41.390
Why do you do such a thing!

16:41.470 --> 16:44.160
What? Why are you
speaking like that?

16:44.400 --> 16:46.170
Then what is this?

16:46.340 --> 16:48.140
Isn't this an embroidery needle?

16:48.610 --> 16:51.040
It was stuck in Naoya's gym clothes!

16:51.110 --> 16:52.580
It was terrible!

16:52.750 --> 16:54.080
You're horrible, Mom!

16:54.380 --> 16:56.970
I'm sorry. I didn't realize.

16:57.450 --> 17:00.750
I guess it got in there
while I was sewing the bag.

17:01.220 --> 17:03.280
I'll be careful from now on.

17:03.560 --> 17:06.180
Are you scared of us that much?

17:06.260 --> 17:07.280
What?

17:07.590 --> 17:09.190
You don't have to hide it.

17:09.260 --> 17:11.990
You can't help but
be scared of us, right?

17:12.200 --> 17:15.360
But just because of that, you don't
have to do something like this!

17:15.530 --> 17:16.930
What are you saying!

17:17.000 --> 17:20.030
You're a lot scarier than us!

17:20.270 --> 17:22.100
No, it wasn't on purpose!

17:22.170 --> 17:23.800
Forget it! Idiot!

17:28.950 --> 17:30.040
What's going on?

17:30.520 --> 17:32.880
What did you guys do to Mom!

17:32.950 --> 17:35.250
You don't like how we're right?

17:35.320 --> 17:36.850
What are you saying, Naoto!

17:36.920 --> 17:38.750
We know, liar!

17:39.160 --> 17:42.790
He's always thinking why
weren't we normal kids.

17:43.030 --> 17:45.390
The truth is he wants us gone!

17:46.830 --> 17:48.230
I can't take this anymore!

17:51.070 --> 17:52.900
I don't want this anymore!

17:53.270 --> 17:55.300
It should just all be burned!

17:55.370 --> 17:56.810
All of this!

18:14.530 --> 18:15.650
Honey!

18:15.860 --> 18:17.090
What happened?

18:25.700 --> 18:27.000
You kids...

18:27.540 --> 18:29.940
This house should just be gone!

18:30.080 --> 18:32.200
Everything should just
burn and disappear!

18:32.280 --> 18:33.640
Dad, you liar!

18:33.710 --> 18:34.970
Mom, you liar!

18:35.350 --> 18:36.710
Everything, disappear!

18:36.780 --> 18:38.770
Everyone should just die!

18:41.250 --> 18:43.590
It's a lie! This is a false memory!

18:43.660 --> 18:45.350
A false memory?

18:45.460 --> 18:51.560
Then who can prove that what is in
your head right now is the true memory?

18:51.930 --> 18:54.130
This is the real memory?

18:54.300 --> 18:56.360
Is that why the house wasn't there?

18:56.740 --> 18:59.600
Meaning our parents
are dead already?

19:03.110 --> 19:04.130
Damn it!

19:27.270 --> 19:29.360
You showed us the fake memory.

19:29.440 --> 19:33.340
No, this is a memory you guys made.

19:33.440 --> 19:35.500
It's your memory.

19:35.570 --> 19:37.630
No! You made it up!

19:38.680 --> 19:42.740
Then why isn't the house there?

19:42.880 --> 19:45.710
Did you guys burn it down?

19:46.990 --> 19:48.950
The past changed!

19:50.120 --> 19:54.220
Then why do you think
the past changed?

19:54.430 --> 19:55.890
It's your doing!

19:56.060 --> 19:57.960
You're saying I did it?

19:59.400 --> 20:01.730
I did it? I myself did it?

20:03.900 --> 20:05.730
Stop it! What's so funny?

20:06.610 --> 20:10.670
You guys weren't wishing for
the existence of your parents.

20:10.880 --> 20:14.900
So I made you guys' wish come true!

20:14.980 --> 20:17.920
You wouldn't understand our suffering!

20:19.620 --> 20:24.060
Man, you haven't comprehended
anything, have you?

20:24.120 --> 20:25.180
What?

20:28.530 --> 20:31.460
You guys have strong powers.

20:32.230 --> 20:37.070
And that power is big enough
to change the real world.

20:37.140 --> 20:38.260
That's why...

20:38.340 --> 20:40.740
That's why I'm here!

20:41.070 --> 20:42.130
Damn it!

20:52.790 --> 20:53.410
Brother!

20:53.750 --> 20:55.480
Brother, are you okay?

21:16.140 --> 21:18.540
Just what is going on?

21:18.710 --> 21:20.700
Who is that guy?

21:21.410 --> 21:23.240
And our memories...

21:23.880 --> 21:25.780
I don't get it, Brother.

21:25.880 --> 21:28.180
I don't know what's going on.

21:28.690 --> 21:31.420
Transition... What is it really?

22:03.920 --> 22:05.950
Is something wrong, Mr. Kamiya?

22:09.190 --> 22:12.060
I just saw the worst future.

22:12.560 --> 22:15.120
The vision of the
downfall of mankind...

22:17.270 --> 22:18.290
Mr. Kamiya...

22:19.870 --> 22:22.570
Naoto Kirihara and Naoya Kirihara...

22:23.410 --> 22:25.470
These two are dangerous.

22:29.920 --> 22:38.720
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:47.560
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

22:47.630 --> 22:56.410
<i>A single shadow looked like light
in this world that I'm imprisoned in.</i>

22:56.480 --> 23:05.210
<i>The rain of May became lighter
as it was kindly shining tomorrow.</i>

23:05.280 --> 23:09.620
<i>I lost the meaning of smiling...</i>

23:09.690 --> 23:13.990
<i>... that day I thought I
lost my place to be.</i>

23:14.060 --> 23:18.430
<i>I wished for your warmth.</i>

23:18.500 --> 23:22.930
<i>We have stopped time.</i>

23:23.170 --> 23:27.260
<i>I had this feeling it was
eventually going to come, but...</i>

23:27.340 --> 23:31.900
<i>... I pretended I didn't know
and buried my loneliness.</i>

23:31.980 --> 23:42.080
<i>I looked down at your feet as the
droplets describing "Good-bye" fell.</i>

23:42.720 --> 23:51.460
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

23:51.530 --> 23:59.900
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

24:01.940 --> 24:05.840
A man named prophet who
is able to see into the future...

24:06.650 --> 24:10.140
A specific scene of destruction
from synchronized tuning...

24:10.720 --> 24:14.910
That is a pain of irrationality
named transition.

24:15.820 --> 24:19.260
For the evasion of a future of
nothingness, we hurry toward...

24:19.320 --> 24:22.050
...the person who is an
essential member of the calamity.

24:23.230 --> 24:29.900
<i>Episode 9, "Annihilation."</i>

24:26.130 --> 24:29.130
Where are we headed?
